<article class="env-lemma" id="03YI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03YI">Lemma <span data-tag="03YI">8.5.3</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $p : \mathcal{S} \to \mathcal{C}$ be a stack. Let $p' : \mathcal{S}' \to \mathcal{C}$ be the category fibred in groupoids associated to $\mathcal{S}$ constructed in Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/03WQ" data-tag="03WQ">4.35.3</a>. Then $p' : \mathcal{S}' \to \mathcal{C}$ is a stack in groupoids. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Recall that the morphisms in $\mathcal{S}'$ are exactly the strongly cartesian morphisms of $\mathcal{S}$, and that any isomorphism of $\mathcal{S}$ is such a morphism. Hence descent data in $\mathcal{S}'$ are exactly the same thing as descent data in $\mathcal{S}$. Now apply Lemma <a href="/tag/02ZF" data-tag="02ZF">8.4.2</a>. Some details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>